WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:06.480
Language is a beautiful thing the human brain
has equipped us with.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.540
We understand and describe the experience
of life in the form of language.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:18.450
It is the conduit for transmitting thoughts
and ideas from human to human, consciousness

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:25.470
to consciousness, producing a worldly vibration
of interconnectivity.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:32.290
But language’s necessity for human social
function has possibly limited the human experience

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.890
of life.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.520
We seem to so often forget that there is a
world beyond our current language.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:46.940
A world of feelings and thoughts that go beyond
linguistic comprehension.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.660
Did depression exist before man created a
term for it?

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.820
Did blue exist before man classified it?

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.270
Did anything exist before man identified it?

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:06.370
If at one point in human history there was
no word for depression, were humans still

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.540
depressed without knowing it?

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.210
What did this unawareness result in?

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:17.960
And what are we feeling right now without
knowing what to call it?

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.360
Without being able to identify it.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.630
Or perhaps the opposite, what aren’t we
feeling because we haven’t yet created any

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.070
words for it?

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:35.840
Our understanding of life and consciousness
is facilitated by language, but our EXPERIENCE

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.070
of life and consciousness does not have to
be limited to it.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:48.049
Life is not solely found in how you think
or speak about it, but also in how you feel

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:49.080
it.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:56.950
It is this that we must understand and try
to embrace as we navigate through life’s

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.570
unknown.

